s the second person to  announce that she wants the job along  with mp pierre pauliev more people are  expected to join in the coming days  though including former quebec premier  josh charles eric sorenson looks at his  chances at becoming the next tory leader  he was one of the brightest young stars  at a time when the conservative  political universe was at its zenith the  1980s charismatic fluently bilingual and  so highly regarded prime minister brian  mulroney made john charret the youngest  cabinet minister in canadian history as  we say in french  zombie in the 90s cheray became leader  but only after the party had collapsed  bringing about the reform party in the  block quebecois he helped rebuild the  party and many credit his oratory for  lifting the no vote in quebec's  referendum on independence  [Applause]  he would go on to become the premier of  quebec for nine years then seemingly  left politics for good that's really our  responsibility to be that national  political party  now he's back he hinted last week at  what he thinks he can do for the party  broaden its appeal one thing that i  believe to be very important is to have  a national conservative party  that is able to represent every part of  canada he took over the party at a time  when rebuilding and outreach were  required and he went on to become  premier of quebec our second largest  province in canada so he knows how to  campaign he knows how to build it he  knows how to win shariah was the focus  of a corruption investigation during his  days as premier and others suggest he is  yesterday's man not the right choice for  a modern conservative party we have to  repudiate conservatives like jean  charret who have an inferiority complex  and want to always act like liberals in  pursuit of trying to win power others  see it differently we are an inclusive  party we should be a welcoming party  and we should also be looking at all  parts of the country for success in the  next election chade 